  "description_short": "Family-run Italian eatery in George serving authentic homemade pasta and wood-fired pizzas.",
  "description_long": "Tucked into the New Virgin Active Building on York Street, Osteria Tre Nonni brings genuine Italian hospitality to George. This family-run spot specializes in traditional dishes made from scratch daily—think hand-rolled pasta, wood-fired pizzas with properly blistered crusts, and generous portions that feel like Sunday lunch at nonna's house.\n\nThe atmosphere strikes a comfortable balance between casual and warmly welcoming, making it equally suited for midweek dinners or leisurely weekend meals with family. The kitchen takes pride in authentic preparation methods, and it shows in the quality of their carbonara, seafood linguine, and classic Margherita pizzas. Located in Dormehls Drift, it's a neighborhood gem that's built a loyal following among locals who appreciate honest Italian cooking without pretense.\n\nWhether you're after a quick pizza or settling in for a proper Italian feast, the consistently good food and reasonable prices make this a reliable choice in George's dining scene.",
